VendorPulse live production notes with port change

Real repo structure on server

/var/www/vendorpulse
├── app/
├── bootstrap/
├── config/
├── database/
├── deploy/
├── public/
├── resources/
├── routes/
├── storage/
├── tests/
├── vendor/
├── web_dashboard/
├── mobile_dashboard/
├── artisan
├── composer.json
├── package.json
├── docker-compose.yml
├── Dockerfile
└── .env

Meaning
- Laravel backend = /var/www/vendorpulse
- Next.js frontend = /var/www/vendorpulse/web_dashboard
- Do not create separate backend/ and frontend/ folders for this repo.

Can this run on the same server as exportdoc?
- Yes.
- Run VendorPulse as a separate Docker Compose stack.
- Do not reuse exportdoc app containers.
- Do not reuse exportdoc database/schema.
- Keep separate domain routing, env, volumes, and compose project name.

Port conflict notes
- docker-compose.yml binds the Laravel app as ${APP_PORT}:8000.
- If 8000 is already used by exportdoc or another app, use APP_PORT=8001.
- Next.js dev commonly uses 3000, but production should be served through the public domain and reverse proxy.
- The public domain stays normal HTTPS; the internal app container can sit on 8001.

Recommended live env file
- Start from: deploy/liveproduction.env.template
- Copy it to: /var/www/vendorpulse/.env

Important .env values for production

APP_ENV=production
APP_DEBUG=false
APP_URL=https://vendorpulse.veravalonline.com
APP_PORT=8001

WEB_DASHBOARD_URL=https://vendorpulse.veravalonline.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://vendorpulse.veravalonline.com/api/v1
NEXTAUTH_URL=https://vendorpulse.veravalonline.com

CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://vendorpulse.veravalonline.com
SANCTUM_STATEFUL_DOMAINS=vendorpulse.veravalonline.com
SESSION_DOMAIN=vendorpulse.veravalonline.com
SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE=true

Database guidance
- Use a dedicated VendorPulse database only.
- If Postgres runs inside the same compose stack, keep:
	DB_HOST=postgres
	DB_PORT=5432
- If Postgres runs on host or managed service, set the real host and port.
- Never point VendorPulse to exportdoc database.

Fresh deployment on Ubuntu live server

1. Go to the project
cd /var/www/vendorpulse

2. Create production env
cp deploy/liveproduction.env.template .env
nano .env

3. Start isolated Docker stack
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose up -d --build

4. Run Laravel setup inside container
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose exec app php artisan optimize:clear
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose exec app php artisan migrate --force
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose exec app php artisan optimize

5. Check services
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose ps
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose logs --tail=100 app
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose logs --tail=100 horizon
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose logs --tail=100 scheduler

If an old VendorPulse Docker setup already exists
- Yes, remove and recreate it cleanly.
- Do not touch exportdoc containers.

Stop only old VendorPulse stack
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose down --remove-orphans

If you want a full fresh reset and do not need old VendorPulse DB data
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose down -v --remove-orphans

Then recreate cleanly
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose up -d --build

Reverse proxy / domain routing
- vendorpulse.veravalonline.com should proxy to VendorPulse app upstream.
- If APP_PORT=8001, proxy to 127.0.0.1:8001.
- Keep exportdoc.veravalonline.com pointing to the existing exportdoc upstream.

Fast checks before cutover
ss -ltnp | grep :8000
ss -ltnp | grep :8001
ss -ltnp | grep :3000

Post-deploy checks
- Login from dashboard.
- Confirm no CORS errors.
- Confirm NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL points to the production API.
- Confirm Horizon is running.
- Confirm scheduler is running.
- Confirm monitoring writes new logs.

Rollback
- Switch reverse proxy back to old upstream.
- Optional: stop VendorPulse stack
	COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=vendorpulse-prod docker compose down

Important reminder
- Do not rely on manual edits made inside running containers.
- Keep real configuration in repo files and the host .env file.
